Pomera third-party firmware notice
===================================

This Debian/Ubuntu root filesystem and the Pomera kernel images include third-party
wireless firmware and regulatory data. They are distributed for use with the
Broadcom wireless hardware in the King Jim Pomera DM200, DM250, and DM250US.

The files retain their original contents. They are not covered by the Linux
kernel GPL license; their own copyright and redistribution terms continue to
apply. See SOURCES.md for the source URLs and checksums, and
LICENCE.broadcom_bcm43xx for the Broadcom license text.

Packaged Wi-Fi firmware is supplied by firmware-brcm80211 (Debian) or
linux-firmware-broadcom-wireless (Ubuntu). Its installed package copyright
file is retained under /usr/share/doc/PACKAGE/copyright. Board NVRAM and
Bluetooth firmware are separately supplied by the pinned Armbian source.

The wireless-regdb package's ISC copyright notice is installed separately at
/usr/share/doc/wireless-regdb/copyright.
